IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lb74-nouns`
IMPORT `lb74-cross-references`

-- Row il-74. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound references kept beside the cited one. They pass.
-- C1: the amendment of SH 2232 names section 2 of the 2005 law, and section 2 of that law is the section SH 2036 prints the first period in: the extension names the same temporary provision whose period the first instrument prints.
-- C2: the title of the National Insurance Law that section 1 of SH 2036 prints equals the title that item 1 of the Third Schedule prints (string equality).
-- C3: the section item 1(e) names is the section SH 2036 section 1 adds.
-- C4: items (a) to (d) name sections 9, 123, 213 and 222(d); the row does not read them, so each is typed NotChecked. Section 213 is also the section paragraph (e) of section 230B applies to the committee's decisions; the row types that as printed text and checks nothing against it.
-- C5: the instruments are typed Printed and dated in the order of their footers.
-- The expected values are hand-written from the quotation lines in lb74-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the values there.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- C1. SH 2232 section 1 amends "section 2", and section 2 is where SH 2036 prints the first period.
#ASSERT `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B`'s `the section of the 2005 law the instrument amends` EQUALS "2"
#ASSERT `the first period printed for section 230B`'s `the section of the instrument that prints it` EQUALS "2"
#ASSERT `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B`'s `the section of the 2005 law the instrument amends` EQUALS `the first period printed for section 230B`'s `the section of the instrument that prints it`
#ASSERT (`the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B`'s `the instrument`'s `the issue date its footer prints`) GREATER THAN (`the first period printed for section 230B`'s `the instrument`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)

-- C2. The title of the National Insurance Law, as section 1 of SH 2036 prints it and as the opening words of item 1 of the Third Schedule print it.
#ASSERT `the title of the National Insurance Law as SH 2036 section 1 prints it` EQUALS `the title of the National Insurance Law as item 1 of the Third Schedule prints it`
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the cited law, as the opening words of the item print it` EQUALS `the title of the National Insurance Law as SH 2036 section 1 prints it`

-- C3. The section item 1(e) names is the section SH 2036 section 1 adds, and the row has read that section's addition.
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the number of the cited section, with letters in Latin` EQUALS "230B"
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the number of the cited section, with letters in Latin` EQUALS `the number of the provision` `National Insurance Law section 230B`
#ASSERT `the provision is added by an instrument deposited here` `National Insurance Law section 230B`
#ASSERT NOT (`the provision was not read` `National Insurance Law section 230B`)

-- C4. Items (a) to (d) name four sections, none of them read by the row.
#ASSERT count `the sections that items (a) to (d) of item 1 of the Third Schedule name` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT all `the provision was not read` `the sections that items (a) to (d) of item 1 of the Third Schedule name`
#ASSERT map `the number of the provision` `the sections that items (a) to (d) of item 1 of the Third Schedule name` EQUALS LIST "9", "123", "213", "222(d)"
#ASSERT NOT (elem "230B" (map `the number of the provision` `the sections that items (a) to (d) of item 1 of the Third Schedule name`))
#ASSERT `the provision was not read` `National Insurance Law section 9`
#ASSERT `the provision was not read` `National Insurance Law section 123`
#ASSERT `the provision was not read` `National Insurance Law section 213`
#ASSERT `the provision was not read` `National Insurance Law section 222(d)`
#ASSERT NOT (`the provision is added by an instrument deposited here` `National Insurance Law section 213`)
-- Paragraph (e) of section 230B applies section 213; item 1(c) names the same number.
#ASSERT elem (`the number of the provision` `National Insurance Law section 213`) (map `the number of the provision` `the sections that items (a) to (d) of item 1 of the Third Schedule name`)
#ASSERT `the number of the provision` `National Insurance Law section 213` EQUALS "213"

-- C5. The instruments are typed Printed, and the footers date them in the order 2036, 2232, 2350, 2387, 2647.
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2036`'s `its status as the row types it` EQUALS Printed
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2232`'s `its status as the row types it` EQUALS Printed
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `its status as the row types it` EQUALS Printed
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2387`'s `its status as the row types it` EQUALS Printed
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2647`'s `its status as the row types it` EQUALS Printed
#ASSERT (`Sefer HaChukim 2036`'s `the issue date its footer prints`) LESS THAN (`Sefer HaChukim 2232`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)
#ASSERT (`Sefer HaChukim 2232`'s `the issue date its footer prints`) LESS THAN (`Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)
#ASSERT (`Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the issue date its footer prints`) LESS THAN (`Sefer HaChukim 2387`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)
#ASSERT (`Sefer HaChukim 2387`'s `the issue date its footer prints`) LESS THAN (`Sefer HaChukim 2647`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)

-- The pages print no calendar date for the commencement day of the first period, nor for the commencement of SH 2350: each answer is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the first period printed for section 230B`'s `the calendar date the words print for the commencement day` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the commencement day that section 18(a) of SH 2350 prints as a calendar date` EQUALS NOTHING
